WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.000
And you, Israel, what does your Lord ask of you if he sees your Lord, to go in all his ways and love him and worship your Lord with all your heart and soul?

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:54.000
We have come together to pay homage to a courageous man. A man who believed in the Tora. A man who seerat ʾAdonai, the fear of God, burnt always in his neshama.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:22.000
He was an example. And to be honest, sometimes I felt embarrassed that I was not able to come to the standards of this man.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:39.000
He was controversial because the truth is controversial. Some people dislike him because we dislike the truth.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:53.000
Some people were envious because not all of us could live our life fully, completely.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Ner L'ragli Deva-lecha.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Shelomo Amalek says, your ner, your torch, God, sheds light upon my steps. The light of God. What is the light of God?

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:37.000
Shelomo hammelekh says, there is a light of God that we all have. Ner ʾAdonai Nishmat ʾAdam.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:49.000
God blew inside us a light. And that light is the Neshama that we have.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:03:03.497
When we wake up in the morning we say Elohai my Lord Neshama Senatata Bi Tehora

00:03:03.497 --> 00:03:09.497
You have endowed me with a pure soul.

00:03:09.497 --> 00:03:23.497
It is a challenge, this Berakha, because sometimes we realize that we have stained that pure Neshama.

00:03:23.497 --> 00:03:47.497
Victor Zakai, head and a Shemaʿ Tehorah. And that's why some people, rather than emulate him, hide themselves in excuses.

00:03:47.497 --> 00:04:08.497
Yes, it's true. He studied Tora at Torat Barat. Yes, it's true. He was an engineer. But you know what he did? He combined engineering with Torat Barat.

00:04:08.497 --> 00:04:16.497
It's easy to have Tora in the abstract. It's so simple.

00:04:16.497 --> 00:04:34.497
Pletitudes. But he was an engineer. An engineer means that you are devoted to implement with actions your theories.

00:04:34.497 --> 00:04:48.497
And what he did throughout his life was engineering institutions, questions, problems, aims for Tora.

00:04:48.497 --> 00:05:03.497
Not platitude. Build structures that would benefit ʿAm Yiśraʾel. You know what? I envy his courage.

00:05:03.497 --> 00:05:16.497
You know what? I envy the lucidity of a man who was afraid of none except Boreʾ ʿOlam.

00:05:16.497 --> 00:05:27.497
This is a poem of Yoḥanan Llevi, so great. He says, Lo E'eros Beltoh, Kilo Adisa.

00:05:27.497 --> 00:05:51.497
The other one says, I fear no one except Him, because I am afraid of Him. Fear of God free us from servitude to platitudes, to men who have no sight for the future.

00:05:51.497 --> 00:06:01.994
Victor Lakai called me last Friday a few I think a day or so before he passed away

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:18.994
And it was Aleph Shabbat, I was in Netanya, and he called me before I wasn't home, that I come, I'm almost ready to go to Bet hakkenesset, and he calls me again.

00:06:18.994 --> 00:06:25.394
And he asked me a question. Now that I don't mention the name for this,

00:06:25.394 --> 00:06:36.594
X, Mr. Raḇaʾ X, passed away, should I drop my suit or I should continue with the suit?

00:06:36.594 --> 00:06:43.394
And I said, drop the suit. Drop the suit.

00:06:43.394 --> 00:06:59.394
He believed that Tora is justice. And therefore, if necessary, bring it to the highest level institutions that you can.

00:07:00.394 --> 00:07:10.394
We who have less of this pristine fervor, it's a pristine, it's the Nishamate Tora, yes.

00:07:10.394 --> 00:07:28.394
Yes, not all of us will have the courage. I said to him, forget about it. Because we realize it's unfortunate that sometimes truth does not prevail.

00:07:28.394 --> 00:07:35.394
I want to say two things. This symbolizes the Brick of Zakkai.

00:07:35.394 --> 00:07:43.394
I met him a couple of years ago in Yerushalayim, and we go to synagogue El Shabbat.

00:07:43.394 --> 00:07:52.394
The synagogue of a friend of mine, the son of Raḇ Shalom, R. Yishak Nisim.

00:07:52.394 --> 00:07:59.394
We go there, we sit down. Before I introduce him to Moshe Nisim, he sees a watch.

00:07:59.394 --> 00:08:08.394
He says, you know, the watch should not be there, because there is no symmetry. It should be moved to the other place.

00:08:08.394 --> 00:08:21.394
And you know what to say. Moshe Nisim, former minister of justice, a man of this, he says to him, you know, move the watch from here and put it there.

00:08:21.394 --> 00:08:29.394
And Moshe Nesim was like that. He said, you are right! You are right! Thank you! And then I introduced him.

00:08:29.394 --> 00:08:41.394
So that is Victor Zakai. He knows how to make things better. He knows how to improve things.

00:08:41.394 --> 00:08:49.394
And I am going to say something that I disagree with. With the mood.

00:08:49.394 --> 00:09:05.491
David Ahmed says Emet me tismah The truth shall come forth from the earth

00:09:05.491 --> 00:09:15.491
What does it mean, Emet me'eres tismah? Well, the truth sometimes is like a seed.

00:09:15.491 --> 00:09:30.491
You see the seed? You pay no attention. You don't worry. What is the seed? It's nothing. So what happened? We buried the seed. We stepped on the seed.

00:09:30.491 --> 00:09:44.491
And as the time passes, it starts growing. It's a flower. It's a tree. It bears fruits.

00:09:44.491 --> 00:09:53.491
And I disagree with you. You think that Victor Zakai passed away? Wrong!

00:09:53.491 --> 00:10:02.491
His neshama, his Peulot, his actions, they are the seed of neshama Terorah.

00:10:02.491 --> 00:10:11.491
We may forget about it, but here and there, we are going to see beautiful flowers, trees,

00:10:11.491 --> 00:10:21.491
bearing outstanding fruits, and his vision will be part of our legacy.

00:10:21.491 --> 00:10:31.991
I pray to Goro ʿOlam that his Zechut should be always over the shoulders of his son ʾEliyahu, his son Semih.

00:10:31.991 --> 00:10:36.491
By the way, your father always told me about you both, alright? And he says about Semih,

00:10:36.491 --> 00:10:42.491
Oh, he's studying yeshiḇa and this and that and all this thing, alright? He was so proud of his children.

00:10:42.491 --> 00:10:47.491
Zechuto tagen alehem, amen, keneh nason. Kon tuv lachem.

00:10:51.491 --> 00:10:55.491
Sages are reciting the Tumar.

00:11:21.491 --> 00:11:51.471
Sages.

00:11:51.491 --> 00:11:53.491
Amey, Ramey.
